<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to December 9 to offset a rise in bank notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   416.024 (+ 0.952)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  15.657 (+ 2.538)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  3.285 (+ 0.049)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.815 (unch)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 103.800 (- 1.737)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   453.585 (+ 4.448)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
